<title>USA: Gateway says wait on Advanced Logic ended.</title>
<headline>Gateway says wait on Advanced Logic ended.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH SIOUX CITY, S.D. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gateway 2000 Inc said the Hart-Scott-Rodino waiting period its $15.50-per-share cash tender offer for all outstanding common shares of Advanced Logic Research Inc ended early.</p>
<p>&quot;The waiting period was terminated by the (U.S.) Federal Trade Commission and the Department of Justice on June 27, 1997,&quot; said the maker and direct marketer of personal computer products.  </p>
<p>Gateway said June 19 it planned to acquire Advanced Logic for about $194 million, marking a move for the PC direct marketer into the potentially lucrative business computer server market.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
